    "source": "-- Proofs, Checked — Chapter 4: common mistakes.\n-- INTENDED TO FAIL. Each theorem contains a deliberate mistake\n-- discussed in the \"Common mistakes\" section of the chapter.\n--\n--   cargo run -p hol_cli -- --course courses/proofs-checked.json --section ch04 docs/book/code/ch04-mistakes.ctea\n\nmode constructive\n\nsort Person\nsort Pet\n\nconst alice : Person\nconst rex : Pet\n\npred Happy(Person)\n\n-- Mistake 1: a witness of the wrong type. The goal asks for a Person,\n-- and rex is a Pet.\ntheorem wrong_witness : Happy(alice) -> exists x : Person, Happy(x) := by\n  intro h\n  exists rex\n  exact h\n\n-- Mistake 2: trying to swap quantifiers the wrong way. `cases ... with\n-- | intro ...` opens an EXISTS; it cannot conjure a single witness out\n-- of a forall. (Good thing, too: the statement is false — see the\n-- chapter.)\ntheorem everyone_has_an_admirer_so_someone_admires_everyone\n  (A : Type)\n  (R : A -> A -> Prop)\n  : (forall y : A, exists x : A, R(x, y)) -> exists x : A, forall y : A, R(x, y) := by\n  intro h\n  cases h with\n  | intro w hw =>\n      exists w\n"
