    "name": "ch05-mistakes.ctea",
    "source": "-- Proofs, Checked — Chapter 5: common mistakes.\n-- INTENDED TO FAIL. Every theorem in this file contains a deliberate\n-- mistake discussed in the \"Common mistakes\" section of the chapter.\n--\n--   cargo run -p hol_cli -- --course courses/proofs-checked.json --section ch05 docs/book/code/ch05-mistakes.ctea\n\nmode constructive\n\nsort Person\n\nconst clark : Person\nconst superman : Person\n\npred Flies(Person)\n\n-- Mistake 1: rewriting in the wrong direction. The goal mentions\n-- `clark`, but `rewrite <- h` hunts for the equation's RIGHT side.\ntheorem wrong_direction : clark = superman -> Flies(superman) -> Flies(clark) := by\n  intro h\n  intro hs\n  rewrite <- h\n  exact hs\n\n-- Mistake 2: refl on an equation that is simply false.\ntheorem arithmetic_optimism : 2 + 2 = 5 := by\n  refl\n\n-- Mistake 3: `have` states one equality, the proof provides the other.\ntheorem have_backwards : clark = superman -> superman = clark := by\n  intro h\n  have h2 : superman = clark := h\n  exact h2\n\n-- Mistake 4: comparing things of different types.\ntheorem type_confusion : clark = 0 := by\n  refl\n"
