    "name": "ch05-exercises.ctea",
    "source": "-- Proofs, Checked — Chapter 5: exercises.\n-- Replace each `sorry` with a real proof.\n--\n--   cargo run -p hol_cli -- --course courses/proofs-checked.json --section ch05 docs/book/code/ch05-exercises.ctea\n\nimport ../../../std/prelude.ctea\n\nmode constructive\n\nsort Person\n\nconst clark : Person\nconst superman : Person\nconst kal_el : Person\n\npred Flies(Person)\npred Reporter(Person)\n\nfunc mother : Person -> Person\n\n-- Exercise 5.1 (warm-up). Let the checker do the arithmetic.\ntheorem ex5_1 : 3 * 4 = 12 := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.2. Computation with a variable in the way.\ntheorem ex5_2 (n : Nat) : n + 2 = succ(succ(n)) := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.3. Equality is symmetric — one lemma, or one rewrite.\ntheorem ex5_3 : superman = clark -> clark = superman := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.4. Chain two equations. Try the `have ... :=` form with\n-- eq_trans, even if you can see a shorter route.\ntheorem ex5_4\n  : clark = superman -> superman = kal_el -> clark = kal_el := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.5. Substitute into a predicate. Watch the direction: the\n-- goal mentions `clark`, the left side of the equation.\ntheorem ex5_5 : clark = superman -> Reporter(superman) -> Reporter(clark) := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.6. Rewrite every occurrence at once.\ntheorem ex5_6\n  : clark = superman\n    -> Flies(superman) /\\ Reporter(superman)\n    -> Flies(clark) /\\ Reporter(clark) := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 5.7. Equal people have equal mothers.\ntheorem ex5_7 : superman = kal_el -> mother(superman) = mother(kal_el) := by\n  sorry\n"
