    "source": "-- Proofs, Checked — Chapter 6: exercises.\n-- Replace each `sorry` with a real proof.\n--\n--   cargo run -p hol_cli -- --course courses/proofs-checked.json --section ch06 docs/book/code/ch06-exercises.ctea\n\nimport ../../../std/prelude.ctea\n\nmode constructive\n\nsort Student\n\nconst ana : Student\nconst ben : Student\n\npred TakesCS(Student)\npred TakesMath(Student)\n\ndef CS : Set Student := { x : Student | TakesCS(x) }\ndef Math : Set Student := { x : Student | TakesMath(x) }\n\n-- Exercise 6.1 (warm-up). Membership in a named set.\ntheorem ex6_1 : TakesMath(ben) -> ben in Math := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.2 (warm-up). Membership in a finite set is a disjunction.\ntheorem ex6_2 : ana in {ana, ben} := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.3. Element chasing across two operations.\ntheorem ex6_3 : inter(CS, Math) subset union(CS, Math) := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.4. The difference stays inside the left set.\ntheorem ex6_4 : diff(CS, Math) subset CS := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.5. Feed the subset hypothesis an element it accepts.\n-- (After the intros, `apply h` turns the goal `x in C` into a goal\n-- about union(A, B).)\ntheorem ex6_5 (T : Type) (A B C : Set T)\n  : union(A, B) subset C -> A subset C := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.6. Set equality: the four-line ritual, then both directions.\ntheorem ex6_6 (T : Type) (A : Set T) : union(A, A) = A := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.7. Taking away nothing changes nothing.\ntheorem ex6_7 (T : Type) (A : Set T) : diff(A, empty(T)) = A := by\n  sorry\n\n-- Exercise 6.8 (challenge). Double complement — one inclusion is\n-- constructive, the other needs a Chapter 3 move. The mode line below\n-- grants permission.\nmode classical\n\ntheorem ex6_8 (T : Type) (A : Set T) : compl(compl(A)) = A := by\n  sorry\n"
