    "kind": "mistakes",
    "label": "Mistakes (meant to fail)",
    "name": "ch08-mistakes.ctea",
    "source": "-- Proofs, Checked — Chapter 8: common mistakes.\n-- INTENDED TO FAIL. Every theorem in this file contains a deliberate\n-- mistake discussed in the \"Common mistakes\" section of the chapter.\n--\n--   cargo run -p hol_cli -- --course courses/proofs-checked.json --section ch08 docs/book/code/ch08-mistakes.ctea\n\nimport ../../../std/prelude.ctea\n\nmode constructive\n\nsort Person\n\npred AgeIs(Person, Nat)\n\n-- Mistake 1: offering the input as a witness for the output. The goal\n-- wants an age (a Nat); x is a Person.\ntheorem witness_from_wrong_column\n  : (forall p : Person, exists n : Nat, AgeIs(p, n)) -> Total(AgeIs) := by\n  intro h\n  unfold Total\n  intro x\n  exists x\n  exact h x\n\n-- Mistake 2: confusing single-valued with injective. The two\n-- definitions differ only in WHICH argument is repeated — and the\n-- checker catches the swap at the exact spot the arguments cross.\ntheorem single_valued_is_not_injective (A : Type) (G : A -> A -> Prop)\n  : SingleValued(G) -> Injective(G) := by\n  intro h\n  unfold Injective\n  intro x1\n  intro x2\n  intro y\n  intro h1\n  intro h2\n  exact h x1 x2 y h1 h2\n\n-- Mistake 3: \"inverting\" succ with truncated subtraction. y - 1\n-- looks like a predecessor, but at y = 0 it is 0, and succ(0) is not 0.\ntheorem succ_surjective_wish : Surjective(fun x y : Nat => succ(x) = y) := by\n  unfold Surjective\n  intro y\n  exists y - 1\n  refl\n"
